# Trivy ignore list — each entry MUST carry a justification + exposure note.
# Reviewed 2026-10-31. Only genuinely-unfixable-or-not-exploitable items belong
# here; everything else must be fixed, not suppressed.

# --- Starlette CVEs whose ONLY fix is Starlette 1.x ---
# FastAPI (even latest 0.120.x) pins `starlette<0.50.0`, so we cannot adopt the
# 1.x fix lines without FastAPI itself moving to Starlette 1.x (future upstream).
# We DID fix the one 0.49.x-addressable CVE (CVE-2025-62727) by pinning
# starlette==0.49.2. The two below are accepted with the exposure noted:
#
# CVE-2026-48818 — StaticFiles SSRF / UNC-path credential theft.
#   Exposure: our only StaticFiles mount serves the built SPA /assets dir
#   (server-controlled, no user-supplied paths); the SPA catch-all has a
#   path-containment guard (main.py). Not reachable with attacker-controlled input.
CVE-2026-48818
#
# CVE-2026-54283 — request.form() size limits silently ignored (form DoS).
#   Exposure: the app enforces its own request-body-size cap in the security
#   middleware (1MB JSON / 50MB upload via Content-Length), which bounds this.
CVE-2026-54283

# NOTE: Litestream was upgraded v0.3.13 -> v0.5.17 (2026-10-31) to clear ~60
# stale Go-stdlib/x-crypto findings from the old build — NOT suppressed here.
# Re-review this file whenever FastAPI adopts Starlette 1.x (then remove the two
# Starlette entries and bump starlette).
